#
# Method: re-audit the post-rename, post-split, post-prefix, post-deadcode-cleanup LSP
# state with full negative trust. Treat the 4 prior audit records as claims to be
# falsified. The 4 passes created a "normalization" effect — each fixed the most
# visible issues but the layered fixes left drift in (a) function/file prefix
# alignment, (b) dead code that became invisible when callers shifted, (c) Academy
# header doc drift, (d) lsp_text.oo not adopted by siblings, (e) cross-layer stubs.
#
# Result: 3 CRITICAL broken refs, 1 STALE compat, 1 DUPLICATE fn, 4 PREFIX
# families (25+ fns), 26+ DEAD fns, 5+ DUPLICATE text utils, 3 re-HEURISTICS,
# 1 MANUAL struct, 9+ STALE doc drift, 6 OTHER minor.
#
# Result: 3 CRITICAL broken references, 1 STALE compat layer, 1 DUPLICATE function,
# 4 PREFIX-MISMATCH families (25+ fns), 26+ DEAD functions, 5+ DUPLICATE text utils,
# 3 re-introduced HEURISTICS, 8 MANUAL struct constructions, 9+ STALE doc-drift items.
# 30+ new findings. The LSP daemon WILL FAIL TO START in `ooda lsp` mode in its
# current state. See companion file for full per-finding details.

# ## 1. CRITICAL — BROKEN BUILD (3 unresolved references)
#
# C1: lsp_server_build_index undefined
#   - lsp_stdio.oo:90, 114 call lsp_server_build_index(fs, env, explicit_root).
#   - Post-rename audit said it was a duplicate and should be deleted; the function
#     WAS removed from lsp_server_handlers.oo but the call sites in lsp_stdio.oo
#     were never updated. Every `ooda lsp` invocation fails.
#   - Fix: replace both with lsp_server_refresh_index(fs, env, explicit_root).
#
# C2: lsp_compile_scan_user not imported
#   - lsp_hover.oo:227 calls lsp_compile_scan_user(content, base).
#   - The function is defined in oodac/api_lsp.oo:60 (different file, different
#     layer). lsp_hover.oo imports lsp_compile.oo, not oodac/api_lsp.oo.
#   - Fix: move to ooda/lsp/lsp_compile.oo, add import to lsp_hover.oo.
#
# C3: lsp_index_from_module undefined
#   - lsp_stdlib_scan.oo:174 calls lsp_index_from_module(&tbl).
#   - Not defined anywhere. lsp_scan_via_compiler depends on it.
#   - Fix: implement in lsp_compiler_merge.oo.

# ## 2. CRITICAL — STALE COMPAT LAYER
#
# S1: oodac/api_lsp.oo is a parallel stub LSP bridge (89 lines).
#   Duplicates all 7 Lsp* struct defs (already in lsp_types_symbol.oo). Stub
#   lsp_compile_module returns empty after checks, no walk. Stub
#   lsp_compile_residual returns list_new() after checks, no walk. TIME BOMB:
#   any caller importing oodac/api_lsp.oo gets the STUB, not the real
#   lsp_compile.oo implementation. 5 trivial lsp_module_*_count getters.
#   Fix: delete oodac/api_lsp.oo entirely.

